MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The HDMI cable fits my TV and Blu-ray setup because it could serve as a useful spare, and its extra length could help me connect existing equipment.",
    "The memory cards fit my history of buying removable storage and a card reader. The 64GB card interests me more than the 32GB option for its additional capacity, provided my intended device supports it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older Echo Dot, Echo Show and Fire TV devices repeat functions covered by my recent newer-device interactions, so their familiarity does not give me a reason to choose them now.",
    "The older Fire tablet offers no clear benefit alongside my recent Echo Show use, while the wired earbuds do not address the computer and home-device accessory needs reflected in my recent activity."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in Alexa devices seems to have been taken as a reason to want more Alexa devices, even when they are older versions of devices I recently interacted with.",
    "My electronics activity seems to have been interpreted too broadly: buying practical accessories does not mean that any familiar electronic device or audio accessory is useful to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The generations and timing of my recent device interactions matter: an older streaming stick or smart display is less compelling after a newer version, especially with my recent Show stand purchase.",
    "I often look for items that support or maintain equipment I already use, such as replacement remote batteries, adapters and cables. Compatibility and a specific added benefit matter more than simply matching a device family."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in electronics accessories but too often treated recent device interest as a need for older, overlapping devices."
}
